;; Docs for std/bench/store.bjo, read through (:doc #:file "store.bjodoc").
;; The texts are samizdat markup: code in prose is @code{...}.

(:doc #:module
  (summary "Benchmark runs as data: written to a file and read back, and compared, with a saved run or in A/B rounds.")
  (see SavedRun write-saved-run! read-saved-run compare-runs compare-paired)
  (example """
    (import (std bench store))

    (match (read-saved-run "base.bjodat")
      ((Ok saved) (compare-runs saved this-run 0.05 0.02))
      ((Err why) (println why)))
    """)
  (reference """
    What @code{--save FILE}, @code{--compare FILE} and @code{bjo bench
    --against} are made of. @code{(std bench)} measures and prints; this
    module knows runs only as data, so that the two do not import each
    other.

    @strong{The file} is one bjodat form, a case to a line, so that a diff
    of two saved runs says which cases changed:

    @codeblock[#:lang "text"]|{
    (bench-run
      (version 1)
      (saved "2026-10-16T12:00:00Z")
      (machine "95c59c6948245e2e")
      (header (build "Release") (dotnet ".NET 10.0.4") (cpu "...") ...)
      (case (name "sort") (labels ("n" "1000")) (k 512) (once #f) (bytes 0.0) (samples [41213.0 ...])))
    }|

    Every sample is kept, in nanoseconds per call and in the order taken,
    rather than a summary: a comparison needs the distribution.

    @strong{A comparison} reports, per case, the change in the median, its
    95% interval, a p-value corrected for the number of comparisons by
    Holm's method, and a verdict. The verdict is @code{Faster} or
    @code{Slower} only when the corrected p is below the level @em{and}
    the change is larger than the threshold; a real change smaller than the
    threshold is @code{SmallChange}.

    A comparison with a saved run is unpaired, and treats the samples of
    each run as independent. Two processes of one program can differ by
    more than a threshold of 2%, so such a comparison can call a difference
    between processes a change; @code{compare-paired} with several process
    pairs measures that difference instead.
    """))

(:doc SavedCase
  (summary "One benchmark at one combination of its parameters, as a saved run keeps it.")
  (field name "The benchmark's name.")
  (field labels "Its parameters, name and value, as the report shows them.")
  (field k "The calls in each sample.")
  (field once "#t for a benchmark of single cold runs.")
  (field bytes "Bytes allocated per call.")
  (field samples "Nanoseconds per call, in the order the samples were taken.")
  (see SavedRun case-key))

(:doc SavedRun
  (summary "A benchmark run: when and where it was taken, and its cases.")
  (field saved "When it was saved: UTC, ISO 8601, to the second.")
  (field machine "The machine key: a hash of the CPU, the core count, the memory and the operating system.")
  (field header "The facts of the machine and the build, by name: build, dotnet, arch, cores, gc-server, cpu, os and governor.")
  (field cases "What was measured.")
  (see SavedCase write-saved-run! compare-runs))

(:doc case-key
  (summary "What a case is known by across runs: its name and parameters, as the report shows them.")
  (arg c "The case.")
  (returns "@code{\"sort n=1000 order=random\"}, or the name alone without parameters."))

(:doc saved-run->string
  (summary "The text of a saved run: one (bench-run ...) form, a case to a line.")
  (arg r "The run.")
  (returns "The text, ending in a newline.")
  (see parse-saved-run write-saved-run!))

(:doc parse-saved-run
  (summary "Reads a saved run from its text.")
  (arg text "The text.")
  (returns "The run, or what is wrong with the text: not bjodat, not a (bench-run ...), a newer version of the format, or a case that lacks something.")
  (see saved-run->string read-saved-run))

(:doc write-saved-run!
  (summary "Writes a run to a file, replacing what was there.")
  (arg path "The file.")
  (arg r "The run.")
  (see read-saved-run))

(:doc read-saved-run
  (summary "Reads the run saved in a file.")
  (arg path "The file.")
  (returns "The run, or a sentence saying what is wrong: no such file, unreadable, or not a saved run.")
  (see write-saved-run! compare-runs))

(:doc Verdict
  (summary "What a comparison concludes about one case.")
  (case Faster "Significant after the correction, and faster by more than the threshold.")
  (case Slower "Significant after the correction, and slower by more than the threshold.")
  (case SmallChange "Significant, and smaller than the threshold: there, and decided not to matter.")
  (case NoChange "Not significant.")
  (see Comparison))

(:doc Comparison
  (summary "One case compared: the medians, the change and its interval, the p-values and the verdict.")
  (field name "The benchmark's name.")
  (field labels "Its parameters.")
  (field was "The median per call of the earlier side, A or the saved run, in nanoseconds.")
  (field now "The median per call of the later side, B or this run.")
  (field change "The ratio of now to was, less one: 0.05 is 5% slower.")
  (field lo "The low end of the change's 95% interval.")
  (field hi "The high end.")
  (field p-raw "The p-value as the test gave it.")
  (field p "The p-value corrected by Holm's method for the comparisons of the run.")
  (field verdict "What it comes to, with the run's level and threshold.")
  (field spread "With several process pairs, the standard deviation of their log ratios; -1 when it was not measured.")
  (see CompareResult Verdict))

(:doc CompareResult
  (summary "Two runs compared.")
  (field comparisons "The cases both have, compared, in the later run's order.")
  (field only-now "The keys of the cases only the later side has.")
  (field only-saved "The keys of the cases only the earlier side has.")
  (field warnings "The facts of the two runs that differ and move times: the build, the .NET version, server GC, the governor.")
  (field other-machine "#t when the machine keys differ: the numbers mean little and no verdict is to be believed.")
  (see compare-runs compare-paired))

(:doc compare-runs
  (summary "A run compared with a saved one, case by case: unpaired, by the Mann-Whitney U test and a bootstrap of the ratio of the medians.")
  (arg saved "The earlier run.")
  (arg now "The later run.")
  (arg alpha "The significance level of a verdict: 0.05.")
  (arg threshold "The smallest change a verdict counts, as a fraction: 0.02.")
  (returns "The comparison.")
  (see compare-paired CompareResult))

(:doc PairedCase
  (summary "One case of an A/B run: each process pair's samples of A and of B, a sample of each a round.")
  (field name "The benchmark's name.")
  (field labels "Its parameters.")
  (field a "For each process pair, A's nanoseconds per call in the order of the rounds.")
  (field b "The same for B, round for round.")
  (see compare-paired))

(:doc compare-paired
  (summary "An A/B run compared, A as was and B as now, paired by round or by process pair.")
  (arg cases "The cases both sides have.")
  (arg only-a "The keys of the cases only A has.")
  (arg only-b "The keys of the cases only B has.")
  (arg alpha "The significance level of a verdict.")
  (arg threshold "The smallest change a verdict counts, as a fraction.")
  (returns "The comparison.")
  (see compare-runs PairedCase)
  (reference """
    With one process pair, the rounds are the pairs: the Wilcoxon
    signed-rank test on each round's log ratio, and the paired bootstrap.
    A drift that moved both of a round's samples moves neither. What it
    cannot see is a difference between the two processes as a whole.

    With several, each pair gives one ratio of medians, and the test is a
    t-test on their logs, with a t-interval: the difference between
    processes is then in the test, and its size is @code{spread}.
    """))
